      "title": "Post-demerger, Vedanta declares first interim dividend of ₹5 per share",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/post-demerger-vedanta-declares-first-interim-dividend-of-5-per-share-126100800678_1.html",
      "description": "Vedanta Ltd on Thursday declared an interim dividend of Rs 5 per share for the current financial year, amounting to about Rs 1,955 crore.\nThis is the company's first interim dividend post-demerger, reinforcing the company's focus on delivering value to shareholders as it enters a new phase as a more focused and diversified natural resources company, the company stated in an exchange filing.\n\"... the board of directors of Vedanta Limited have, today, i.e. October 08, 2026, approved the first interim dividend 2026-27 of Rs 5 per equity share on face value of Rs 1 per equity share for the financial year 2026-27 amounting to Rs 1,955 crore,\" Vedanta said in the filing.\nThe dividend comes soon after a strong Q2 FY27 operational performance, with Vedanta reporting broad-based momentum across its businesses. The company recorded record quarterly and half-yearly production across key operations, with particularly strong performance in zinc, ferro alloys, ports and aluminium.\nThe performanc",
